  "primary_public_sources": [
    "https://whatsappbusiness.com/policy/"
  ],
  "policy_checked": "Current primary WhatsApp Business Messaging Policy, last modified September23,2026, checked October1,2026. Opt-in and opt-out plus approved templates outside the customer-service window; recent relationship alone is not permission.",
  "findings": [
    "Campaign eligible audience includes unconfirmed and subscribed states; available recipients do not prove channel/destination/message-type permission. Import consent applies to new contacts; deduplicated existing contact retains own state.",
    "Small tests need explicit authorization and isolated destinations/conditions; draft, preview, acceptance and delivery are different stages. No sending performed for editorial work.",
    "One clear action; final personalization, links and channel-specific unsubscribe need end-to-end verification. SMS draft does not prove WhatsApp active approval.",
    "Business-local quiet hours and per-flow frequency policies differ; they do not automatically enforce a universal recipient-local cap for every campaign and route.",
    "Capture naming identifies configured tool/report, not proof of origin, consent or attribution of every deduplicated profile.",
    "Tags menu shows profile fields/kept properties; optional values may be empty, contextual tags depend on flow.",
    "Closing conversation has real lifecycle/capacity/follow-up/CSAT effects. Do not close unresolved work to cosmetically improve metrics.",
    "Campaign period is anchored to reporting launch; sent/delivered/engaged and conversion are different populations. Engaged counts delivered messages with seen/click/reply, grouped by business-local dispatch day, later signals may update cohort. Attribution windows and total/unique clicks differ."
  ],
  "execution": "Source read-only and GitHub content fetches. No examples or app actions performed."
}
